# Shared Mailbox Security Standard

## Purpose

Define the security model for role-based addresses such as sales, billing, support, and info.

## Standard

Shared mailboxes are service mailboxes, not human identities.

## Requirements

- Do not distribute shared mailbox passwords
- Block direct interactive sign-in for the underlying user object where applicable
- Delegate mailbox access to named user accounts
- Grant only the permissions required:
  - Full Access
  - Send As
  - Send on Behalf, only where explicitly needed
- Remove delegated access promptly when staff roles change
- Review mailbox permissions periodically

## Current Kile Business Systems shared addresses

- sales
- billing
- support
- info

## Future-state operating model

As staff are hired, each employee receives an individual Microsoft 365 account. Shared mailbox permissions are assigned to that named account according to job function.

## Security rationale

This preserves accountability because actions are tied to authenticated named identities rather than a shared password.
